  "7518886051856150528": {
   "created": 1792642128,
   "author": "Ken N.",
   "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/kennielsend_massive-ai-debt-systemic-crisis-not-so-activity-7518886051856150528-e1JL",
   "text": "Massive AI debt = systemic crisis? Not so fast.\n\nBlackstone\u2019s Jas Khaira says the real story is different. It\u2019s a financing gap \u2014 not a 2008-style banking meltdown.\n\nWhy that matters:\n\n\ud83d\udd39 Blackstone\u2019s playbook is compute-first. It launched Blackstone N1 in San Francisco and is deploying debt, equity and bespoke capital structures to fund data centers, neoclouds and chip plays.\n\n\ud83d\udd39 Examples worth noting:\n- CoreWeave: a $2.3B loan in 2023 against Nvidia GPUs and blue-chip customer contracts. That model scaled into follow-on debt.\n- Crux AI: $5B commitment to commercialize Google TPUs via a neocloud partnership.\n- Other deals: co-leading a $10B facility for Firmus and backing early chip startups ",
