  "7518914403145019392": {
   "created": 1792648888,
   "author": "Next in Branding",
   "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/next-in-branding_dvc-venturebranding-nextinbranding-activity-7518914403145019392-AknD",
   "text": "\ud83d\udca5 DVC by Daniil Sergeev\n\nWhat does a venture fund look like when the portfolio is the proof and the community is the product?\n\nDVC operates at a genuinely interesting intersection in the AI investment landscape: 190+ investors, 120 backed startups, and a portfolio that includes Perplexity AI, Etched, and Thinking Machines Lab \u2014 the kind of names that do considerable brand work on their own. But the identity brief goes deeper than portfolio credentials. A fund managed by a family of founders, built around a community of engineers, founders, and angels, is a fundamentally different organism than a traditional venture structure. The multilayered color cluster visuals understand that distinction",
