   "added": 1792767922
  },
  "7519395232694804480": {
   "created": 1792763527,
   "author": "AI Insider",
   "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/ai-insider-intel_ai-aiinfrastructure-datacenters-activity-7519395232694804480-gdu-",
   "text": "Blackstone is positioning itself at the center of AI financing, from data center loans to frontier models.\n\nSpeaking at TechCrunch Disrupt, Jas Khaira, who leads the firm\u2019s San Francisco AI hub Blackstone N1, described it as the largest owner of compute outside the hyperscalers, citing a $5B commitment to Crux AI, built with Google around its TPUs, and an investment in Etched.\n\nBlackstone pioneered GPU-backed neocloud lending with a $2.3B CoreWeave loan and co-led a $10B facility for Firmus.\n\nKhaira acknowledged rising rates and heavy debt have rattled markets but dismissed comparisons to 2008, noting most data center debt is backed by creditworthy hyperscalers. \n\nThe firm is also driving ad",
